{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Rjb4kBp2p99w61XogoC55","type":"tool_result","content":"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D23 post-run, 2026-10-23)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning (history, compressed): D1-D8 identity/image/pdf/zip basics; D9-D15 Windows binaries/installers/\nshortcuts/Office (PE x3 days -> .NET -> MSI -> LNK -> OOXML); D16 e-mail; D17 audio + D18 video (one `media.*` stream\nproperty each, ffprobe vocabulary); D19 ELF, D20 Mach-O (thin; raw `0x` cputype list), D21 Android APK (`package`), D22\nJava JAR (`Main-Class`). Since D17 EVERY family lasted exactly ONE day and one field; the flavor's promised depth\n(transcodes, crops, fat slices, clones, nested launchers) was never delivered in any mode. Timed kits are cumulative\n(+1 field/day) with a 5-name sha256 synthesis; D22 Mastery grew to SIX sets.\n**D22 \"Main Character Energy\" = JAR** (`jar.main_class` -> `Main-Class` verbatim; prebuilt race hit ~19 s).\n**D23 \"Page Me Maybe\" = SQLite** (`sqlite.page_size_bytes` of one `database-001.sqlite`, 12 288 B = 3 x 4096; header\nu16 BE @16, `1` = 65536; id `d23-sqlite-001-sqlite-...`, plain fmt `sqlite`). The D16-night prebuild `sqlite-header`\nanswered it in the race probe (~29 s). Flavor: \"Application databases have been copied, truncated, embedded, and\nmislabeled. Validate page geometry, connect databases to parent applications, and find the impossible claim.\" ->\nunasked siblings: in-header size vs file length (truncation), magic at a non-zero offset (embedded), extension lies,\napplication_id / schema fingerprint -> parent app, header claims that cannot be true (version number, page size, WAL\nflag without WAL). **D23 timed MUTATED the whole carry-over kit** (fat Mach-O, shuffled CD, Ogg/MP3 audio, non-x86\nPE/ELF machines, re-rolled identity sizes) and taught that EVERY json list is answered SORTED (CD order rejected).\nProgression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 turned to APPLICATION DATA. D24-D26 most plausibly: (a) another\napplication data store -- ESE/JET (SRUM, WebCache, Windows.edb), LevelDB/IndexedDB (Electron/Chrome apps), SQLite WAL\n/ journal, plist/bplist app prefs (prebuilt), Realm/LMDB/Access/dBase; (b) a deeper SQLite field if the one-day\npattern breaks (application_id, user_version, page_count, text encoding, table names -- all prebuilt); (c) the Windows\nDFIR block (EVTX / registry hive / prefetch / $MFT / jump lists / recycle bin -- all prebuilt) for D26-D31, plus\nPCAP / X.509 / disk images (prebuilt). The flavor depth lands in the TIMED mutations of carried families, so keep every\ncarried extractor general (multi-slice, multi-stream, both byte orders, every codec).\n\n## 1. Atlas\n\n| # | Concept / field | Status | Recognition cues | Standard tool / lib + exact call | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Identity: filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | seen D1 (+D15 member roster) | any member; id stem names WHICH member | `hashlib.<algo>(b).hexdigest()`; `sha256sum` (I) | high -- every timed kit |\n| 2 | `file.magic_prefix_hex_N` | seen D2 | first N bytes | `xxd -p -l 16` (I); `b[:N].hex()` | high (carry-over) |\n| 3 | `text.utf8_bom_present` (utf16 sibling speculative) | seen D3 | `ef bb bf` / `ff fe` / `fe ff` | `b.startswith(codecs.BOM_UTF8)` | high (carry-over) |\n| 4 | `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` | seen D4 | `ff d8 ff`; SOFn `ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc | segment walk; `identify -format %wx%h` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 5 | `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` | seen D5 | `89 50 4e 47 0d 0a 1a 0a`; IHDR @12 | `struct.unpack('>II', b[16:24])`; `pngcheck -v` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 6 | `pdf.header_version` | seen D6 | `%PDF-x.y` @0 | `b[5:8]`; `pdfinfo` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 7 | `zip.eocd_total_entries` | seen D7 | `PK\\x05\\x06` last; u16 @+10 | struct; `7z l -slt` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 8 | `zip.central_directory_member_names` (SORTED ascending) | seen D8 + D23 (D23 TT: stored CD order REJECTED once the CD was shuffled; sorted CORRECT -- D8-22 disks were already sorted) | `PK\\x01\\x02` walk, name @+46 | `sorted(zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(b)).namelist())` -> compact JSON | high (carry-over) |\n| 9 | `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` | seen D9 | `MZ`, e_lfanew @0x3C, `PE\\0\\0` | `pefile.PE(data=b).FILE_HEADER.Machine` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 10 | `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` | seen D10 | opt hdr +16 | `pe.OPTIONAL_HEADER.AddressOfEntryPoint` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 11 | `pe.version_original_filename` (+ `pe.version_*` family) | seen D11 | RT_VERSION, `VS_VERSION_INFO` UTF-16 | `pe.FileInfo[..].StringTable[0].entries` (I); `exiftool -j` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 12 | `dotnet.mvid_guid` | seen D12 | data dir 14 -> `B