{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ChYhHYLN1aTZMuN8z5APjG","type":"tool_result","content":"| 148 | Parent-application attribution of a database: application_id (`0x0f055112` Fossil, `0x47504b47` GPKG, `0x4d504258` MBTiles; D23 `0x48545254` 'HTRT'), user_version, schema fingerprints (Chrome \n| 149 | SQLite WAL / rollback journal / shm: WAL `37 7f 06 82/83` header (format 3007000, page size u32 @8, checkpoint seq, salts, frame count = (len-32)/(24+ps), commit frames), journal `d9 d5 05 f9 \n| 150 | Deleted SQLite records: freelist trunk/leaf pages, freeblocks / unallocated space in leaf pages, carved rows (dfir staple) | gap (sqlite-deleted-records) | freelist count @36 > 0; freeblock of\n| 151 | LevelDB / IndexedDB / Chromium Local Storage: `.ldb`/`.sst` footer magic `57 fb 80 8b 24 75 47 db`, `.log` 32 KiB blocks (crc32c, len, type), `MANIFEST-*` VersionEdit (comparator `leveldb.Byte\n| 152 | Other application DB formats: MS Access Jet/ACE (`Standard Jet DB`/`Standard ACE DB` @4, version @0x14), dBase `.dbf` (version byte, YYMMDD last update @1, record count u32 @4, header/record s\n| 153 | Browser profile DBs beyond history: Chrome `Cookies` (host_key, name, expires_utc WebKit, encrypted_value `v10`/`v11` prefix), `Login Data` (origin_url, username_value), `Web Data` autofill, d\n| 154 | Mobile app DBs: iOS `sms.db` (date = ns since 2001 Cocoa epoch), `KnowledgeC.db` (ZOBJECT), Android `mmssms.db` (`sms` date ms since 1970), WhatsApp `msgstore.db`, `contacts2.db`, Signal/Teleg\n\n{\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D20 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set; D20 solver carried the dispatch forward -> timed first try; the 409 pre-fetch body listed DIFFERENT Files than the live attempt). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py. D21: Files grew to FIVE names (note + panel png + managed dll + message eml + mobile-001.apk), same list in all 5 Mastery sets, order re-rolled per set -- never assume a count. D22-D23: Files = FIVE names and DIFFER between sets of one \n\n{\"id\": \"timed-carryover-mutations\", \"concept\": \"Timed kits mutate every carried family; json lists must be SORTED\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT/Mastery re-rolled values that were constant D13-D22: PE Machine 0x01c0/0x01c2/0x01c4/0x01f0/0x0ebc/0x5064/0x8664, ELF e_machine 0x0003/0x0028/0x002b/0x0102, audio mp3/opus/vorbis/pcm_s16le, video dims arbitrary, Mach-O FAT 2-3 slices (0x7, 0xc, 0x12, 0x01000007, 0x0100000c, 0x01000012, 0x0200000c), shuffled zip CD, PDF 1.0-2.0, BOM true, identity sizes 72-378 B, sqlite page 512-65536. lib answered all values right; the two failures were list ORDER: GM wants zip CD names and macho cpu_type_set SORTED ascending (CD order rejected; fat_arch order != accepted) and a local override returned a Python list -> repr. Action for lib/solver owners: one json choke point (sorted + compact) for every `json` answer except `*-synthesis-*-order`; fixture tests with multi-slice fat, shuffled CD, Ogg Opus/Vorbis, MP3, non-x86 PE/ELF so the next carried family (sqlite) is covered for its mutations too (page size 1 = 65536, WAL header, UTF-16 encodings).\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"ese-edb-header\", \"concept\": \"ESE / JET Blue database header (SRUM, WebCacheV01.dat, Windows.edb, ntds.dit) -- next 'application database' family\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt ese (aliases edb, esedb, jet, srum). Header page 0 (LE): checksum u32 @0, signature `ef cd ab 89` @4, format_version u32 @8 (0x620), file_type u32 @12 (0 database, 1 streaming), database_time (8 B) @16, database_signature (28 B: random u32 + log time 8 B + computer name 16 B) @24, database_state u32 @52 (1 JustCreated, 2 DirtyShutdown, 3 CleanShutdown, 4 BeingConverted, 5 ForceDetach) -> state name spelling `clean_shutdown`/`dirty_shutdown` + raw int, format_revision u32 @232, page_size u32 @236 (4096/8192/16384/32768) -- verify every offset against the libesedb format doc before coding, last_attach/detach times (log time = 6 B y/m/d/h/m/s bytes + padding -> ISO-8601), shadow header copy at page 1 (compare -> header_shadow_match). Fields: page_size_bytes, format_version_u32_hex, format_revision_u32_hex, database_state, database_state_name, file_type, page_count (len // page_size, header pages included), is_dirty. Catalog (table names) only if a stdlib page walk fits in ~200 lines: catalog root = page 4 (FDP 2) -> table names MSysObjects, SruDbIdMapTable, {D10CA2FE-...} SRUM GUID tables, Containers (WebCache) -> table_names JSON sorted. Non-ESE -> `none`. Fixtures: synthesize headers with struct (no Windows DB here); `esedbinfo` is missing.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"evtx-records\", \"concept\": \"EVTX record fields (EventID, TimeCreated, Provider, Channel, Computer, count)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt evtx: record_count, first_event_id, first_time_created_utc, provider_names, channel, computer_name) + event_ids (ordered list), last_event_record_id, event_data_<name> family. Blocked by gate-allowlist-dfir-libs unless a stdlib BinXML walker is written (template substitution makes that ~400 lines; widening the allowlist for Evtx is cheaper).\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"sqlite-wal-journal\", \"concept\": \"SQLite WAL / rollback-journal / shm sidecar files\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt sqlite_wal (aliases wal, sqlite) and sqlite_journal (alias journal). WAL: 32-B header BE: magic u32 0x377f0682 (LE checksums) / 0x377f0683 (BE), format version u32 @4 (3007000), page size u32 @8, checkpoint sequence @12, salt-1 @16, salt-2 @20, checksum-1/2 @24/@28; frames = 24-B header {page number u32, db size after commit u32 (non-zero = commit frame), salt1, salt2, cksum1, cksum2} + page. Fields: wal_page_size_bytes, wal_format_version, checkpoint_sequence, salt1_u32_hex, salt2_u32_hex, frame_count ((len-32)//(24+ps)), commit_frame_count, valid_frame_count (salts match header AND cumulative checksum chain valid -- implement the sqlite wal checksum: s0 += x0 + s1; s1 += x1 + s0 over u32 pairs in the magic's byte order), pages_written (sorted unique JSON), last_commit_db_size_pages. Rollback journal: magic `d9 d5 05 f9 20 a1 63 d7`, page count u32 @8 (-1 = compute), nonce @12, initial db size pages @16, sector size @20, page size @24 -> journal_page_count, journal_page_size_bytes, journal_sector_size. shm: wal-index header version 3007000 @0, mxFrame @16, nPage @20. Non-matching -> `none`.\"}\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D23 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D24-D26 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode:\nthe D23 'application databases' flavor siblings (truncation / impossible header claims, parent-app attribution,\nembedded copies) and the NEXT application-data families (ESE/JET, LevelDB/IndexedDB), plus the timed carry-over\nmutation rules (json lists SORTED). The D22 JAR/launcher items dropped to 2 (built; every family since D17 lasted\none day). TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D20 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set; D20 solver carried the dispatch forward -> timed first try; the 409 pre-fetch body listed DIFFERENT Files than the live attempt). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py. D21: Files grew to FIVE names (note + panel png + managed dll + message eml + mobile-001.apk), same list in all 5 Mastery sets, order re-rolled per set -- never assume a count. D22-D23: Files = FIVE names and DIFFER between sets of one Mastery (D23: note/panel png/msi/mp4/sqlite vs note/pdf/lnk/mp4/sqlite) -- parse each set's text; still sha256-only.\"},","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3867642-d13d-49e8-a4b4-6aff32ca6fb9","uuid":"6d79ccc4-e633-4daf-b5cd-147c6c554518","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:24:17.035Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| 148 | Parent-application attribution of a database: app