{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgM8sAjm6QC5k3GViU24y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YXViRrf2aL84Xq2vZKoYoY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=s.index('```json',i); k=s.index('```',j+7)\ng=json.loads(s[j+7:k])\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nfor gid in ('sqlite-integrity-claims','sqlite-app-attribution','sqlite-embedded-carve','leveldb-indexeddb'):\n    by[gid]['priority']=2\nby['ese-edb-header']['concept']=\"ESE / JET Blue database header (SRUM, WebCacheV01.dat, Windows.edb, ntds.dit) -- Windows DFIR block (D24 EVTX) AND application-database family\"\nby['timed-carryover-mutations']['detail']+=\" D24: the D23 fixes held -- TT 29 / Mastery 232 (8 sets) first try while the kit mutated again: audio `ftyp M4A ` -> aac and `fLaC` -> flac (still named audio-001.wav), Mach-O thin LE-32 `ce fa ed fe` (60 B) -> [\\\"0x0000000c\\\"] beside fat 2-3 slices, PE 0x0266 MIPS16, ELF 0x0016 S390 / 0x00b7 AArch64 / 0x00f3 RISC-V, SQLite page 2048, PDF 1.1/1.6/1.7. Expect EVTX to mutate from D25: several chunks, record-id gaps, a dirty header, an empty or zeroed second chunk -- the record_count walk must cover every chunk.\"\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D24: FIVE names (note + document-001.pdf + collector-001.elf + shortcut-001.lnk + events-001.evtx), same five in all 8 Mastery sets, order re-rolled; sha256 only.\"\nby['evtx-records']['detail']+=\" D24 GM-asked `evtx.record_count` (integer; walk every chunk's records to its free-space offset) -- the evtx.py record walk is stdlib. Remaining record fields (event ids, times, providers) still need BinXML: see evtx-event-semantics.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"evtx-record-integrity\",\"concept\":\"EVTX integrity and the 'selectively shortened timeline' (record-id gaps, header vs walk, dirty/truncated logs)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 flavor: 'duplicated, truncated ... Count records accurately and find the selectively shortened timeline'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/evtx_integrity.py, fmt evtx (aliases eventlog, evt_x); reuse the record walk of lib/meta/prebuilt/evtx.py (do not change its verified record_count path). All LE. Per record: magic `2a 2a 00 00`, size u32 @4 (copy at record end), EventRecordID u64 @8, written FILETIME u64 @16. Fields: record_ids (JSON list ascending ints as strings? -> emit compact JSON of ints), first_record_id, last_record_id, record_id_gap_count (number of missing ids between min and max), missing_record_ids (compact JSON sorted), first_missing_record_id (`none` when contiguous), missing_record_count, is_contiguous (`true`/`false`), header_next_record_id, header_next_record_id_matches (`true` iff == last walked id + 1), header_chunk_count, walked_chunk_count (chunks with `ElfChnk\\\\0` magic), empty_chunk_count, chunk_record_count_list, header_is_dirty (flags & 1), header_is_full (flags & 2), header_crc32_valid (zlib.crc32(b[0:120]) == u32 @124), chunk_header_crc_valid (crc32 of chunk[0:0x78] + chunk[0x80:0x200] == u32 @0x7C, all chunks), event_records_crc_valid (crc32 of chunk[0x200:free] == u32 @0x34), truncated (file length < 4096 + header_chunk_count*65536 or a record size crossing EOF), first_written_time_utc / last_written_time_utc (record @16 FILETIME -> ISO-8601 `Z`, sub-seconds dropped), time_span_seconds, time_out_of_order_count (records whose written time < previous by record id). Non-ElfFile -> `none`. Fixtures: build EVTX with struct (header + 1-2 chunks + minimal records with valid size copies) incl. a deleted-middle-record variant and a dirty header.\"},\n {\"id\":\"evtx-event-semantics\",\"concept\":\"EVTX per-event content without python-evtx: EventID, TimeCreated, Provider, Computer, Channel, EventData values\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Gate blocks `Evtx` (gate-allowlist-dfir-libs) so write a stdlib BinXML reader in lib/meta/prebuilt/evtx_binxml.py: tokens 0x0F fragment header, 0x0C template instance (template def offset into the chunk, cached by offset; GUID + data size), 0x01/0x41 open start element (name offset -> chunk string table: hash u16 + len u16 + UTF-16LE), 0x02/0x03/0x04 close, 0x05/0x45 value text, 0x06/0x46 attribute, 0x0D/0x0E normal/optional substitution (index u16, type u8) into the instance's substitution array {size u16, type u8, pad} -> typed values (0x01 string UTF-16, 0x04 u8, 0x06 u16, 0x08 u32, 0x0A u64, 0x11 FILETIME, 0x13 SID, 0x15 hex64, 0x0E binary, 0x21 BinXML nested). Fields (fmt evtx): event_ids (JSON list in record order), distinct_event_ids (sorted JSON), event_id_counts (compact JSON object sorted keys), most_common_event_id, first_event_id, last_event_id, computer_names (sorted distinct), first_computer_name, channel, provider_names (sorted distinct), first_time_created_utc / last_time_created_utc (System/TimeCreated @SystemTime FILETIME -> ISO `Z`), logon_types (4624 LogonType sorted distinct), target_user_names (4624/4625 TargetUserName sorted), new_process_names (4688), service_names / service_image_paths (7045), script_block_text_first (4104), log_cleared (`true` if 1102 or 104 present). Cross-check against python-evtx in fixtures only (worker side). If BinXML parsing fails -> None (not `none`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"evtx-multi-log-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-log synthesis over several EVTX members (duplicates, hosts, the truncated / shortened copy)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 flavor 'logs from several hosts have been duplicated, truncated, and bundled with reports ... find the selectively shortened timeline'. Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_*.py with an evtx module: given the question's `Files: [...]` (or all .evtx members of the container): duplicate_groups (members whose walked record-id+written-time sequences are identical -> sorted JSON of sorted name lists), duplicate_of (name), truncated_member (walk shorter than the header claims / record crossing EOF), shortened_member (the one with record-id gaps; tie -> fewest records), host_groups (Computer of the first record -> {host: sorted names}), record_count_order (names by walked count asc, ties by name), earliest_member / latest_member (first written time). Same synthesis grammar as digest_order (compact JSON names, `case_insensitive`). Depends on evtx-record-integrity (+ evtx-event-semantics for Computer; fall back to the UTF-16 string scan of the first record's template for the Computer value).\"},\n {\"id\":\"regf-dirty-translogs\",\"concept\":\"Registry hive integrity: dirty hive (sequence mismatch), transaction logs, checksum, bins vs size -- D24 'truncated/shortened' flavor applied to the next Windows DFIR artifact\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/regf_integrity.py, fmt regf (aliases registry, hive, ntuser, reg). Base block LE: `regf` @0, primary seq u32 @4, secondary seq u32 @8, last written FILETIME @12, major/minor @20/@24, file type @28 (0 primary, 1 log, 6 log new), root cell offset @36, hive bins data size u32 @40, clustering @44, file name UTF-16 @48 (64 B), checksum u32 @0x1FC = XOR of the first 127 dwords (0 -> 1, 0xFFFFFFFF -> 0xFFFFFFFE). Fields: primary_sequence_number, secondary_sequence_number, is_dirty (`true` iff they differ), checksum_u32_hex, checksum_valid, hive_bins_data_size_bytes, hbin_count (walk `hbin` blocks from 0x1000 by size u32 @8), hbin_walk_size_bytes, truncated (file length < 0x1000 + data size), last_written_time_utc (ISO `Z`), embedded_file_name. Transaction log (.LOG1/.LOG2): base block file type 6 + `HvLE` log entries (size u32 @4, flags, sequence u64 @12, hive bins data size, dirty pages count @20, hash-1/hash-2 Marvin32) -> log_entry_count, log_first_sequence, log_last_sequence; old format `DIRT` dirty vector -> dirty_page_count. Coordinate with existing lib/meta/prebuilt/regf.py (read it first; do not duplicate its fields).\"},\n {\"id\":\"amcache-shimcache\",\"concept\":\"Execution evidence from Amcache.hve and SYSTEM ShimCache (AppCompatCache)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Windows DFIR block, plausible D25-D28. Stdlib regf cell walk (nk `nk` name/subkey list `lf`/`lh`/`li`/`ri`, vk `vk` name/type/data, big data `db`) -- reuse lib/meta/prebuilt/regf.py helpers if present. Amcache (fmt amcache, alias regf): `Root\\\\InventoryApplicationFile\\\\*` values LowerCaseLongPath, FileId (`0000` + sha1 -> emit sha1 lowercase without the 4-zero prefix as `*_sha1`, raw as `file_id`), LinkDate, ProductName, Publisher, Size; fields: application_file_count, file_paths (sorted JSON), sha1_list (sorted), first_file_path, entry_for_<name> lookups via question text. ShimCache (fmt shimcache, aliases appcompatcache, regf): value `ControlSet00N\\\\Control\\\\Session Manager\\\\AppCompatCache\\\\AppCompatCache`; Win10/11 header size u32 @0 (0x30/0x34), entries with `10ts` sig: sig, unknown u32, entry size u32, path len u16, path UTF-16, FILETIME, data size u32, data -> entry_count, paths (in CACHE ORDER -- an order field, emit as stored, NOT sorted; note it), first_path, last_modified_times. Fixtures: build tiny hives with struct.\"},\n {\"id\":\"usn-journal-records\",\"concept\":\"$UsnJrnl:$J change-journal records (file names, reasons, timestamps) -- NTFS sibling of the D24 record-count question\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt usn (aliases usnjrnl, usn_journal, j). $J is sparse: skip zero runs (8-byte aligned). USN_RECORD_V2 (MajorVersion 2): RecordLength u32 @0, Major u16 @4, Minor u16 @6, FileReferenceNumber u64 @8, ParentFileReferenceNumber u64 @16, Usn i64 @24, TimeStamp FILETIME @32, Reason u32 @40, SourceInfo u32 @44, SecurityId u32 @48, FileAttributes u32 @52, FileNameLength u16 @56, FileNameOffset u16 @58 (60), name UTF-16; V3 (Major 3): 128-bit file refs, name offset @0x4C; V4 = ranges (count only). Fields: record_count (walked valid records), first_usn, last_usn, file_names (distinct sorted JSON), first_file_name, reason_flags_set (sorted JSON of USN_REASON names e.g. `USN_REASON_FILE_CREATE`), deleted_file_names (Reason & 0x200 FILE_DELETE, sorted), renamed_pairs (old 0x1000 / new 0x2000), first_time_utc / last_time_utc (ISO `Z`), file_reference_number_hex of a named file (MFT entry = low 48 bits, sequence = high 16). Non-USN -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"eventlog-exports-legacy-evt\",\"concept\":\"Event-log 'reports': Event Viewer CSV/XML/text exports and legacy .evt logs\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 flavor 'bundled with reports'. fmt evt (alias legacy_evt): ELF_LOGFILE_HEADER (HeaderSize u32 0x30 @0, `LfLe` @4, major/minor @8/@12 = 1/1, StartOffset @16, EndOffset @20, CurrentRecordNumber @24, OldestRecordNumber @28, MaxSize @32, Flags @36 (1 DIRTY, 2 WRAP, 4 LOGFULL, 8 ARCHIVE), Retention @40, EndHeaderSize @44); records: Length u32 @0, `LfLe` @4, RecordNumber @8, TimeGenerated u32 epoch @12, TimeWritten @16, EventID u32 @20 (low 16 bits = displayed id), EventType u16 @24, NumStrings @26, EventCategory @28, StringOffset @36, UserSid len/off @40/@44, SourceName + Computername UTF-16 @56; EOF record `11111111 22222222 33333333 44444444`. Fields: record_count (walk, wrap-aware from StartOffset), oldest_record_number, current_record_number, next_record_number, is_dirty, event_ids, source_names, computer_names, first/last time_generated_utc. fmt eventlog_report (aliases csv_report, xml_report, report): Event Viewer CSV (header `Level,Date and Time,Source,Event ID,Task Category`), Get-WinEvent/Export-Csv (`TimeCreated`,`Id`,`ProviderName`,`RecordId`), wevtutil XML `<Events><Event xmlns=\\\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/win/2004/08/events/event\\\">`, wevtutil text `Event[N]:` blocks -> record_count, record_ids (sorted JSON), event_ids, first/last time, computer_names, missing_record_ids. Cross-file: report_vs_log_record_count_mismatch handled by evtx-multi-log-synthesis.\"},\n {\"id\":\"etl-etw-trace\",\"concept\":\"ETW trace logs (.etl): buffer and logfile headers\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt etl (aliases etw, trace). File = sequence of buffers of BufferSize; WMI_BUFFER_HEADER (0x48 B): BufferSize u32 @0, SavedOffset @4, CurrentOffset @8, ReferenceCount @12, TimeStamp FILETIME @16, SequenceNumber i64 @24, ClockType/Frequency @32, ..., BufferType u16, BufferFlag u16 @0x3C-ish (verify against the public `etl-parser` / `ETWTraceLogFile` layout before coding). First event = TRACE_LOGFILE_HEADER (system trace header): BufferSize, Version (major/minor/sub/subminor bytes), ProviderVersion (OS build), NumberOfProcessors, EndTime FILETIME, TimerResolution, MaximumFileSize, LogFileMode, BuffersWritten, StartBuffers, PointerSize, EventsLost, CpuSpeedInMHz, LoggerName/LogFileName (UTF-16 after the struct), TimeZone, BootTime, PerfFreq, StartTime, BuffersLost. Fields: buffer_size_bytes, buffer_count (len // buffer size), buffers_written, events_lost, pointer_size_bytes, number_of_processors, os_version (`major.minor.build`), start_time_utc, end_time_utc, logger_name, log_file_name. Non-ETL -> `none`. Spec-only (no sample here): mark speculative.\"},\n {\"id\":\"customdestinations-ms\",\"concept\":\"CustomDestinations-ms jump lists (concatenated LNK streams)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt customdestinations (aliases custom_destinations, jumplist_custom, jumplist). AppID = the 16-hex filename stem. Header: version u32 @0 (2), category count u32 @4, ...; categories: type u32 (0 custom with name UTF-16 len-prefixed, 1 known (KDC_FREQUENT 1 / KDC_RECENT 2), 2 tasks) + entry count; entries = 16-B CLSID `01 14 02 00 00 00 00 00 c0 00 00 00 00 00 00 46` then a full LNK; footer `ab fb bf ba`. Simpler robust route: carve every `4c 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 00 00 00 00 c0 00 00 00 00 00 00 46` header, parse each with lib.meta.lnk target_path. Fields: app_id, entry_count, lnk_target_paths (JSON list in file order -- order field), first_target_path, category_names (sorted), has_footer. Coordinate with lib/meta/prebuilt/jumplist.py (Automatic variant).\"},\n]\nids={x['id'] for x in g}\nfor n in new: assert n['id'] not in ids\n# insert new priority-1 after ese-edb-header, priority-2 after other-app-db-formats\npos=[x['id'] for x in g].index('ese-edb-header')+1\ng[pos:pos]=[n for n in new if n['priority']==1]\npos=[x['id'] for x in g].index('other-app-db-formats')+1\ng[pos:pos]=[n for n in new if n['priority']==2]\n# stable sort by priority to keep order readable\ng=sorted(g,key=lambda x:x['priority'])\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=s[:j+8]+body+s[k:]\nold_rank=s[s.index(\"Ranking (D23 post-run)\"):s.index(\"```json\",i)]\ns=s.replace(old_rank,\"\"\"Ranking (D24 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D25-D27 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD24 opened the WINDOWS DFIR block with EVTX: its flavor siblings (record-id gaps / header-vs-walk / truncated or\nduplicated logs, event semantics, cross-log synthesis) and the NEXT DFIR artifacts not yet built (registry hive\nintegrity + transaction logs, Amcache/ShimCache, $UsnJrnl, ESE/SRUM) are priority 1, plus the timed carry-over notes.\nThe D23 SQLite flavor siblings and LevelDB dropped to 2 (SQLite lasted one day like every family since D17).\nTARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n# validate\ns=open(p).read(); i=s.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=s.index('```json',i); k=s.index('```',j+7)\ng=json.loads(s[j+7:k]); print(len(g), all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g))\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('metadata-forensics:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') is True or (st.get('metadata-forensics:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts') or 0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pend), pend)\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3173,"cache_read_input_tokens":116156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3173},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3867642-d13d-49e8-a4b4-6aff32ca6fb9","uuid":"83e89e65-4d9b-4f96-9277-5045f9c37bc4","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:26:02.790Z","request_id":"req_011CgM8sATtiYJYACPWnRmkh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YXViRrf2aL84Xq2vZKoYoY":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=s.index('```json',i); k=s.index('```',j+7)\ng=json.loads(s[j+7:k])\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nfor gid in ('sqlite-integrity-claims','sqlite-app-attribution','sqlite-embedded-carve','leveldb-indexeddb'):\n    by[gid]['priority']=2\nby['ese-edb-header']['concept']=\"ESE / JET Blue database header (SRUM, WebCacheV01.dat, Windows.edb, ntds.dit) -- Windows DFIR block (D24 EVTX) AND application-database family\"\nby['timed-carryover-mutations']['detail']+=\" D24: the D23 fixes held -- TT 29 / Mastery 232 (8 sets) first try while the kit mutated again: audio `ftyp M4A ` -> aac and `fLaC` -> flac (still named audio-001.wav), Mach-O thin LE-32 `ce fa ed fe` (60 B) -> [\\\"0x0000000c\\\"] beside fat 2-3 slices, PE 0x0266 MIPS16, ELF 0x0016 S390 / 0x00b7 AArch64 / 0x00f3 RISC-V, SQLite page 2048, PDF 1.1/1.6/1.7. Expect EVTX to mutate from D25: several chunks, record-id gaps, a dirty header, an empty or zeroed second chunk -- the record_count walk must cover every chunk.\"\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D24: FIVE names (note + document-001.pdf + collector-001.elf + shortcut-001.lnk + events-001.evtx), same five in all 8 Mastery sets, order re-rolled; sha256 only.\"\nby['evtx-records']['detail']+=\" D24 GM-asked `evtx.record_count` (integer; walk every chunk's records to its free-space offset) -- the evtx.py record walk is stdlib. Remaining record fields (event ids, times, providers) still need BinXML: see evtx-event-semantics.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"evtx-record-integrity\",\"concept\":\"EVTX integrity and the 'selectively shortened timeline' (record-id gaps, header vs walk, dirty/truncated logs)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 flavor: 'duplicated, truncated ... Count records accurately and find the selectively shortened timeline'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/evtx_integrity.py, fmt evtx (aliases eventlog, evt_x); reuse the record walk of lib/meta/prebuilt/evtx.py (do not change its verified record_count path). All LE. Per record: magic `2a 2a 00 00`, size u32 @4 (copy at record end), EventRecordID u64 @8, written FILETIME u64 @16. Fields: record_ids (JSON list ascending ints as strings? -> emit compact JSON of ints), first_record_id, last_record_id, record_id_gap_count (number of missing ids between min and max), missing_record_ids (compact JSON sorted), first_missing_record_id (`none` when contiguous), missing_record_count, is_contiguous (`true`/`false`), header_next_record_id, header_next_record_id_matches (`true` iff == last walked id + 1), header_chunk_count, walked_chunk_count (chunks with `ElfChnk\\\\0` magic), empty_chunk_count, chunk_record_count_list, header_is_dirty (flags & 1), header_is_full (flags & 2), header_crc32_valid (zlib.crc32(b[0:120]) == u32 @124), chunk_header_crc_valid (crc32 of chunk[0:0x78] + chunk[0x80:0x200] == u32 @0x7C, all chunks), event_records_crc_valid (crc32 of chunk[0x200:free] == u32 @0x34), truncated (file length < 4096 + header_chunk_count*65536 or a record size crossing EOF), first_written_time_utc / last_written_time_utc (record @16 FILETIME -> ISO-8601 `Z`, sub-seconds 